WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:14.660
The significance of this area for me, as a
child I was brought up out here with my family,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:21.200
we'd come out in the seasonal periods and
live on the river and the estuary, gathering

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.450
mahinga kai.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:27.740
Most people are unaware we have a lot of rare
birds out here and not only rare, they're

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.620
in decline.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:40.040
There is roughly seventy bird species recorded
in and around the estuary here.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.860
There are about twelve endemic species that
can be seen here.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.900
For us it is important that it is protected.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:01:01.600
So the bylaw has just been changed for the
estuary and this area, to a no-dog zone.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:07.080
Also we've put into place for no vehicle access
into the estuary.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:15.409
We patrol weekendly, and weekly to just try
and combat against anyone who's not up to

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:19.360
date with the change in the bylaw for vehicles
in the estuary.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.000
Yeah, I think for a lot of them it is just
education.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.780
They don't perhaps realise what damage they're
doing.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:31.960
It's like everywhere you go, 99% of the public
are really good, it's just that 1% that are

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:39.960
out there to be disruptive, and that's where
the local community jump on board with the

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:40.960
new bylaw.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:47.180
They've all had a part, their input, through
the process of the bylaw being put into place,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:53.580
so when they see something happening in their
area, their patch, they'll give us a call

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.980
and we'll come down and deal with the situation.

